# Runtime data — the image ships no user data; /data is a VOLUME populated at
# deploy time. EXCEPT data/constants.json, which is baked-in static config
# (SECTION_ORDER etc.), not user data — inventory_api.py loads it at *import*
# time from a path relative to the module's own directory (not --data-dir),
# so the image needs its own copy regardless of what gets mounted at /data.
# Found the hard way: `docker build` failed at the `import server` sanity
# check with FileNotFoundError('/app/data/constants.json') before this
# exception was added.
data/**
!data/constants.json
# Same reasoning for the rest of the repo-committed data/ assets, which the
# Dockerfile also copies: an exclusion here keeps the file out of the build
# CONTEXT, so its COPY fails the build outright with "not found" — the
# Dockerfile's COPY list and this exemption list have to be kept in step.
# tests/python/test_container_assets.py fails when they drift apart.
# data/dubIS.ico stays excluded on purpose: it is only app.pyw's native
# window icon, read off the local filesystem and never fetched over HTTP.
!data/dubIS.png
!data/digikey-icon.png
!data/lcsc-icon.ico
!data/mouser-icon.svg
!data/pololu-icon.svg
!data/openpnp_families.json

# Test suites, tooling, and docs never needed at runtime.
tests/
node_modules/
docs/
.superpowers/
.claude*
scripts/
tools/
openpnp/

# Playwright / JS test artifacts.
*.spec.mjs
playwright-report/
test-results/

# VCS / misc.
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Editor/OS cruft.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log
